            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SunnyDaysNora"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We enjoyed this! I upped the nuts to a cup and made 8 personal-size cheese balls. They freeze well to put in lunches later with crackers. Next time I would up the horseradish a smidge and follow Pam's suggestion with the mustard.",
            "datePublished": "2014-03-05T13:24:38.853Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "pam taylor"
            },
            "reviewBody": "One of my favorite cheese balls...instead of the mayo, I use plain old bottled mustard. I think it goes better with the corned beef and horseradish. I leave the nuts off and roll in additional minced corned beef. The guys like this one lol.",
            "datePublished": "2013-09-29T20:17:51.700Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ladybuggs5224"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this the other night for a snack and we enjoyed it okay. I wanted more of a dip so I used spreadable cream cheese and left out the walnuts. The flavor is good but this seems to need something else I just can't seem to put my finger on what I would want it to be =). Solid recipe that you could throw just about anything into!",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-10T06:18:34.250Z"
          }
